        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>You can’t complain Intertek’s £10bn takeover happened – the problem is the lack of arrivals in the other direction </p><p>It would be a stretch to describe the £10bn-ish takeover of Intertek as a landmark event for the London stock market or the FTSE 100 index.</p><p>This is not an <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/armholdings\">Arm Holdings</a> moment – the purchase of that Cambridge chip designer by Japan’s SoftBank in 2016 provoked long (and continuing) agonising over the lack of whizzy tech stocks on the London market.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/nils-pratley-on-finance/2026/jun/18/another-ftse-100-firm-falls-private-equity-where-new-listings\">Continue reading...</a>"
